    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (74.76) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.67) leading the offensive charge. **Caminero** draws the premier matchup of the day against Kelly, benefiting from a high SP_xERA of 4.85 and a favorable top-of-the-order slot. **Alvarez** remains an anchor; despite facing a capable arm in Flaherty, his elite xwOBA of 0.444 coupled with a high-leverage No. 2 spot makes him an automatic start. While **Trea Turner** (69.55) faces a slight efficiency tax due to a quick-release catcher, his elite stolen base potential and lead-off positioning secure him as our highest-scoring utility play. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.08) rounds out the strong options, where his high-frequency stolen base profile against a slower delivery pitcher adds significant value in our scarcity-weighted 5x5 framework.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Carson Benge**, who finished with a 39.35 score, just missing our mandated 40.0 floor. While **Benge** holds upside in the lead-off spot, a negative platoon split against a tough arm in Luzardo eroded his efficiency, ultimately keeping him on the bench. We are proceeding cautiously with **Christian Yelich** (56.90); while his lead-off role provides floor stability, his efficiency takes a notable hit against a lefty, and we are monitoring the lineup for any late-breaking weather patterns that could further suppress his output. Conversely, **Lars Nootbaar** (59.47) is a surprising riser; despite a park penalty, his dynamic platoon advantage against Phillips allows him to slot comfortably into our outfield rotation. No further lineup adjustments are expected at this time, though we remain vigilant regarding the confirmed defensive alignment.",
